### Requests for the demo gateway (IntelliJ HTTP client). The demo of Orgkeep must run (Keycloak on 8280, realm demo),
### with greetings-api-spring on 8290 and the gateway on 8292.

### 1. A token of Paul, for the catalogs prod and sandbox. Lightweight once the "Lightweight tokens" switch of the login
# client is on (dashboard, Login client page).
POST http://localhost:8280/realms/demo/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=demo&username=paul&password=password&scope=openid prod sandbox

> {% client.global.set("token", response.body.access_token); %}

### 2. Through the gateway: X-Gateway-Token says introspection, then cache. The API answers how the token it received
# was verified ("jwt (offline)": the full token) and the size of its Authorization header.
GET http://localhost:8292/greetings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3. The same lightweight token, directly to the API, which has no introspection credentials: 401.
GET http://localhost:8290/greetings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
